  <section class="section mist">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="reveal">What the data buyer pays</h2>
      <p class="reveal">If the company becomes a qualified data partner and the deal closes, you receive <strong>$50,000 or 6% of the partnership value, whichever is bigger</strong>.</p>
      <p class="muted small-note reveal">These are the data buyer's stated terms. Your referral is confirmed in writing before any deal moves forward.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section teal-soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="reveal">Who the data buyer is looking for</h2>
      <ul class="checklist reveal">
        <li><strong>30+ full-time U.S. office staff</strong>10+ for accounting, finance or medical firms, 6+ for law firms.</li>
        <li><strong>3+ years of operating history</strong>With those years of records still in the company&rsquo;s systems.</li>
        <li><strong>At least five systems</strong>Email, internal chat, file storage, CRM, plus one more such as finance, calls or operations.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="reveal">More than half of the company&rsquo;s staff must work from U.S. offices, and the company must own the records in those systems.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

